      "text": "Holosystolic: cont. Systol murmur of MV regurg (pansystolic)  As Lt ventricle squeezes, it pushes blood retrograde into Lt atrium =murmur. ventricular P will cont > atrial P throughout systole so sound over MV stays same. murmur starts @ S1 & ends @ S2, when MV/TV completely opens for start of systole. time murmur starts @ beginning systole b/c ⍉ P gradient to overcome like in AS.  "
